To deploy the User Event script in NetSuite, follow these steps:

Upload the Script File:

Navigate to Documents > Files > SuiteScripts.

Click the "Add File" button and upload your .js file to the file cabinet.

Create the Script Record:

Go to Customization > Scripting > Scripts > New.

Select the script file you just uploaded from the "Script File" dropdown list.

Click the "Create Script Record" button.

Provide a descriptive Name (e.g., "Formula Vector Embedding UE") and a custom ID.

Click "Save" to save the script record.

Deploy the Script:

From the newly created script record, click the "Deploy Script" button (or navigate to the Deployments subtab).

In the "Applies To" dropdown field, select your specific Custom Record Type (customrecord_ns_formula_lib).

Set the deployment "Status" to "Testing" (the script will only execute for you as the script owner) or "Released" (the script will execute for all users).

In the "Event Type" field, select "Create" and "Edit" to ensure the script only triggers during those specific actions.

Click "Save" to finalize the deployment.








Step 1: Create the Custom Record Type
Navigate to Customization > Lists, Records, & Fields > Record Types > New.

In the Name field, enter a descriptive name (e.g., "Formula Library").

In the ID field, enter _ns_formula_lib. NetSuite will automatically prepend customrecord to this, resulting in the exact customrecord_ns_formula_lib ID required by the SuiteScript architecture.

Check the boxes for Show in List and Include in Search Menu. This ensures the custom record is available in the "Search Type" list when you need to query it.

Click Save.

Step 2: Create the Custom Fields
Fields are straightforward to create once the record type is established. From the Custom Record Type page you just saved, navigate to the Fields subtab and click New Field for each of the following:

Field 1: Formula Description

Label: Formula Description

ID: _formula_description (NetSuite will convert this to custrecord_formula_description)

Type: Free-Form Text (or Rich Text)

Store Value: Checked

Click Save & New.

Field 2: Formula Syntax

Label: Verified Formula Syntax

ID: _formula_syntax (NetSuite will convert this to custrecord_formula_syntax)

Type: Long Text (NetSuite formulas can be lengthy, so Long Text is required)

Store Value: Checked

Click Save & New.

Field 3: Vector Embedding

Label: Vector Embedding

ID: _formula_embedding (NetSuite will convert this to custrecord_formula_embedding)

Type: Long Text

Store Value: Checked

Recommended configuration: On the Display subtab for this specific field, set the Display Type to Hidden. This prevents users from manually editing or accidentally breaking the raw JSON mathematical array generated by the AI model.

Click Save.

Once these steps are completed, your customrecord_ns_formula_lib schema is fully built and ready to capture the vector embeddings generated by your User Event script.
